[{:coscientist/subject
  "judah Apple M4, kexe-benchmark (isa hoisted), count-loop GMIR, amu 27d69898 / native 4bb08b9 / mir 767d3c0",
  :doc/doc_type "coscientist-iteration",
  :doc/body
  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 29\n\nThis is the first timed ranking of a call+loop: production\n`:call-live` versus the old `:all-vregs` policy, on quiet judah,\nthrough `kotoba-lang/perfgate`. Encodings are not a ranking.\n\nThe iteration-16 24-live pair is call+if already timed in iteration\n17. This file does not rematch that.\n\nDo not overwrite 04-28.\n\n## What was timed\n\nSame GMIR (`call-and-back-edge-module`, export `count-loop`) compiled\ntwice on judah from amu `27d69898` (native `4bb08b9` → mir `767d3c0`).\nThe bytes that ran are the bytes encoded there.\n\n| arm | policy / slots | code bytes | count-loop offset | sha256 |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---|\n| production | `[:call-live 0]` | 92 (kernel 88) | **4** | `d420fd28183a74f36c10728b80e6d7f744ff0bb6dddb7ff70efc47060e346f73` |\n| baseline | `[:all-vregs 8]` | 144 (kernel 140) | **4** | `cba152818b47979d5cf3db27f2f3ce8216eb088835b4220f876a2e283a239bb9` |\n\n`id` sits at offset 0 (4-byte `ret`). Offset 4 is the count-loop\nexport, not a default of 0.\n\nBaseline is not `with-redefs` of `back-edge?`. After iteration 28 that\npredicate is not a routing guard, so redefining it does not change\npolicy. The baseline overrides `allocate-with-policy` so a\ncall-containing function takes `allocate-with-spills` and\n`:all-vregs`. The leaf `id` still takes the production allocator:\nforcing `:all-vregs` on a no-call body is `call-frame-policy-violation`.\nThe short-circuit was not restored into production source.\n\nRunner: `/tmp/kexe-benchmark-iter29` compiled from amu\n`bench/runtime-comparison/kexe-benchmark.c` (`cc -std=c11 -O3 -Wall\n-Wextra -Werror`). n=50, 100k calls, 10k warmup, ISA aarch64.\n\nThis workstation is not a ranking host. Samples ran on **judah**\n(Apple M4 mini, 10 cores, loadavg `{ 1.83 1.66 1.70 }` start and end).\nIteration 17 used `{ 1.61 1.71 1.83 }`. load1 stayed under 4.\n\n## Oracle\n\nHarness `warmup=0` and `n=0` are outside the admitted range\n(`allow_zero` is false for those argv). One-shot used 1 call and 1\nwarmup. Result **50** on both arms, no `KEXE_TRAP`. The same result\nheld on every scored sample. n=0 is the taken exit and is not ranked.\n\n## Times\n\n12 discarded frequency-warmup rotations (two arms rotated), then 25\nscored rotated samples. Judge: **min ns/call** reported; **perfgate\nuses means**.\n\n| arm | min | mean | median | p95 | max | rel stdev |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| prod (`:call-live`) | 39.17 | 39.294 | 39.24 | 39.57 | 39.72 | 0.0037 |\n| all-vreg | 62.44 | 64.675 | 63.77 | 72.63 | 73.85 | 0.0449 |\n\nmin ratio prod/all-vreg **0.627**. mean improvement **+39.24%**.\n\nDump: `/tmp/iter29-dump/` on judah and the workstation\n(`prod.bin`, `allvreg.bin`, `samples.json`, `arms.edn`, `qualify.edn`,\n`claim.edn`).\n\n## perfgate\n\n`perfgate.core/qualify` on the 25 ns/call vectors. Candidate = prod\n(`:call-live`), baseline = all-vreg, metric `:wall-ns`, unit\n`\"ns/call\"`. Machine descriptor `:measured` from `ssh judah sysctl\nhw.ncpu hw.pagesize hw.cachelinesize hw.l1dcachesize hw.l2cachesize\nmachdep.cpu.brand_string` (ncpu 10, pagesize 16384, cachelinesize 128,\nl1d 65536, l2 4194304, brand Apple M4). ways not reported; not\nfabricated.\n\n- mean improvement **+39.24%** (required +5%)\n- gap **25.381 ns** > summed stdev **3.050 ns**\n- relative stdev 0.0037 / 0.0449 (allowed 0.10)\n- `:qualified? true`\n- **claim sealed** fingerprint `1010495960`, machine-id\n  `judah-m4-mini`, machine-fingerprint `1020876766`\n\nThis is a claim that production call+loop `:call-live` beats the old\nall-vreg policy on this mini, on this fixture. It is not a claim that\nLLVM is beaten. The leaf ranking (iteration 14) stays refused. Do not\nrematch leaf vs LLVM. Do not write this ratio into\n`amu/docs/performance.md`.\n\n## Pins\n\nNo pin bump. The ranking used the pins iteration 28 already landed:\n\n- kotoba-mir `767d3c0b418f85d1d177f78b0648c106a79bfb62`\n  west-pin `efebb442d71c3ad6da6d515c8486ea6cdcb5b88f`\n- kotoba-native `4bb08b9228bc41168ab42bf6d7d2e60150104aff`\n  west-pin `82e0ae925b8383dc57380bcb90123d0012b38ee5`\n- amu `27d69898aca60db492d2c415eae31d7a72a07243`\n  west-pin `115ea914ce4a734c8f842a48695dc23a91a8ebb0`\n- perfgate `d4417d77c2333047dd4e478675e5ed13e1c6b1b8` (= origin/main)\n- machine `4f57144aa6d3c240eb23c44dacab0b7ad5f5c505` (= origin/main)\n\n## What this does not change\n\n- Timed `bench` export stays refused (iteration 4 / 5).\n- `:llvm-beaten` remains false. Leaf refusal (14) stands.\n- `:cfg-liveness` remains false. last-uses are still textual.\n- The 24-live call+if pair is already timed in 17.\n- Production source still has no `back-edge?` short-circuit.\n- west pins were not moved.\n\n## Next\n\nThe leftover on this week's timing is instruction selection on leaves\n(kernel_wide / kernel_deep still 1.44–1.62× LLVM on the Air ranking\nthat iteration 14 refused to overwrite). cfg-liveness is still not\nthis week's timing. Do not rematch leaf vs LLVM. Do not overwrite\n04-28.",
